--- Composes a list of functions left-to-right, returning a single arrow.
---
--- @details
--- `flow` takes a list `fs` and returns an arrow equivalent to
--- `x ~> fn(...f2(f1(x)))` -- functions run in list order, reading like
--- a pipeline. For mathematical right-to-left ordering use
--- `comb.compose`; to feed an initial value in directly use `comb.pipe`.
---
--- An empty list yields the identity arrow.
---
--- @example
--- `inc :: x ~> x + 1`
--- `dbl :: x ~> x * 2`
--- `f :: [inc, dbl] >>> comb.flow`
--- `3 >>> f`
--- -- => 8
---
export flow :: fs ~> x ~> while { xs: fs, acc: x } {
  [xs, acc] ~> match xs {
    []: { out: acc },
    [h, ...t]: { state: { xs: t, acc: h(acc) } }
  }
}
